},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)=3u-5v$ and $y(u,v)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+v).$  \n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =3 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =-5 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =\\frac{1}{u+v} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =\\frac{1}{u+v}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{u+v} & \\frac{1}{u+v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (\\frac{1}{u+v})-(-5)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{u+v}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{u+v}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383502 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383503 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383502 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383504 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383502 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383505 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383502 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383506 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383502 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383507 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383502 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383502 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383502 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186383503 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383502 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9dd5cc0a-1c3d-5de1-81cf-3a2da295967f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383503 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{8}{u+v}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383503 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383503 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6c0a2d56-1032-5653-bdf7-fcbbe224983e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383504 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{u}{u+v}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383504 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186