d{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{u}{2})$ and $y(u,v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡v}{2{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{u}{2})} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{u}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡v}{2{cos}^{2}⁡(u/2)} & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{u}{2}) \\\\ \\,0\\, & \\,\\text{ }\\text{ }\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡v}{2{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{u}{2})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385409 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385409 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385411 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385409 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385412 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385409 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385413 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385409 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385414 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385409 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385409 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385409 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186385410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385409 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "46c8b93f-fcc0-528b-abf0-be921590f6fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921863