db/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389188 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-v \\\\ uv+1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-preserving?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389188 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "99972da5-e4e5-5505-b6d1-ad2a467bcb50" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389188 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving at the points where the Jacobian determinant is positive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}>0.\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-v \\\\ uv+1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2u & -1 \\\\ v & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2u\\cdot u-v\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{u}^{2}+v & >0 \\\\ v & >-2{u}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=-2{u}^{2}\n$$\n\ndefines a parabola, and the coordinates of, say, $(1,1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-preserving must be the following:\n\n![](images/8b/8b35fbafaf8d121bceef7a0763253df075fe4fe85eb3c992f95c59d05f986c67.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389189 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389189 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389189 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389189 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186389189 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186389194 #edb